   "use": "Body part + ga itai is the pattern for any pain, usually said without ga: atama itai. Add n da or n desu when it's the reason you can't do something.",
   "notes": "Also used, as in English, for a problem that's a headache.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "asa kara zutto atama itai.",
    "ja": "朝からずっと頭いたい。",
    "english": "I've had a headache since this morning."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "asa kara zutto atama ga itai n desu.",
    "ja": "朝からずっと頭が痛いんです。",
    "english": "I've had a headache since this morning."
   }
  },
  {
