   "use": "Covers any pain in the belly; usually said without ga, onaka itai, often with n da or n desu to explain. Often a polite hint that you need the toilet.",
   "notes": "An upset stomach from something you ate is onaka o kowasu (onaka kowashita). Onaka no choushi ga warui is the discreet way to mention it.",
